      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, a new roof typically costs between\n\n$8,500 and $19,500 for a standard single-family home using architectural asphalt shingles. The absolute average for a mid-sized home lands around $14,800, but prices fluctuate dramatically based on your home's square footage, chosen materials, and roof complexity.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between $8,500 and $19,500"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost by Home Size"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Most roofing contractors in Utah price projects by the square foot (ranging from $4.50 to $8.25 installed for standard shingles). Below is a general cost breakdown by home square footage:",
