        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Utah-Specific Cost Factors"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Location: Due to higher labor market rates and architectural complexities, homes in Salt Lake County ($9,000\u2013$20,000) typically cost more to re-roof than homes in Cache County\n($8,500\u2013$18,000)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Pitch & Snow Load: Utah requires sturdy roof structures to withstand heavy winter snow loads. If your home has a steep pitch or complex valleys, labor costs will increase due to safety setup requirements.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              5,
              9,
              10,
              11
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-off Layers: Utah building codes limit how many shingle layers can safely sit on a roof. Tearing off multiple layers of old shingles usually adds $1 to $3 per square foot to your estimate.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6,
              7,
              12,
              13
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Decking Repair: If winter moisture or old leaks have rotted your underlying plywood (OSB decking), replacing those sheets will add to your base quote."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8,
          14,
          15,
          16
        ]
      },
